<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-Wells Fargo estimates cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Wells Fargo estimates cut.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brown Brothers Harriman analyst Raphael Soifer cut his earnings per share estimates, on an as-reported basis, to $14.50 and $18.25 for 1997 and 1998, respectively, down from our former estimates of $16.00 and $20.75, which had been based on more optimistic revenue numbers.</p>
<p>-- Soifer said he cut his estimates because of continued transitional problems relating to Wells Fargo's acquisition of First Interstate.</p>
</text>
